ven interval.    \n\nFrom the given graphs, the only curve that is concave up on $[1,4]$ is the one shown below.\n\n![](images/d3/d31008777c9ef9f1f72175f922a2d7c42660796e8c3ffa1dc29198727e8c5734.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392676 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2960d2d6-7354-5f2a-80cc-8d514465455f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether the Trapezoidal Rule Sum Gives an Underestimate or Overestimate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "210d83c3-7a5f-5665-b5c2-daead8591781" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e0/e048c1c1052238e83f1c74864e4806371e0fa8c2c2f3499b6e244614f14aeb76.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392678} {:answer/id #uuid "e8f1f5f2-9232-5218-9446-6da440aee018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2f/2f966ea4bc8d2257a9082347c1bf774cbb40f0c2b5561a0d051fe088bdab43d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392679} {:answer/id #uuid "c565c814-24a3-5363-a559-bd3be2f5b15e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/54/546afec9a47772181b933cb26afda052e5f039226c02db0c565b3e06b0418458.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392680} {:answer/id #uuid "f4966d18-8ba2-5a56-8bd4-5d1a3b25f287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/025a9032c02e58fba378b41936f3f7191251bd14ba1e63c2d199a5352ce7494b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392681} {:answer/id #uuid "f919a43e-ea4c-5056-bf0d-7a796ccc14a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d1/d11a3557cddc21f5f20f4c85374fa2ca7bddf70307671542f228874af64585d4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392682}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8f1f5f2-9232-5218-9446-6da440aee018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2f/2f966ea4bc8d2257a9082347c1bf774cbb40f0c2b5561a0d051fe088bdab43d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392679} :answer-field/id #uuid "df901850-5b4c-5250-a9cd-0821b7975975" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5f7cda04-70ae-570b-9bd1-8ebb0e1d2784" :question/math-academy-id "q-49165" :question/problem "For which of the following graphs would the trapezoidal rule give an underestimate of the area under the curve between $x=-2$ and $x=2?$" :question/worked-solution "The trapezoidal rule underestimates the area under the curve if the function is concave down over the given interval.     \n\nFrom the given graphs, the only curve that is concave down on $[-2,2]$ is the one shown below. \n\n![](images/2f/2f966ea4bc8d2257a9082347c1bf774cbb40f0c2b5561a0d051fe088bdab43d2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097270 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdc82e49-5df6-5096-a8fd-e00017fb1e3a" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Definite Integral as the Limit of a Left Riemann Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75a85318-b190-5737-a110-a53c2d61116f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[2{(3+\\frac{i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392684} {:answer/id #uuid "4f87f8d4-091f-597f-8064-57217d4058eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[2{(1+\\frac{4i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392685} {:answer/id #uuid "e85e3aa9-96ed-523b-82db-3d9bbeb770fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[2{(1+\\frac{i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392686} {:answer/id #uuid "ee49c490-8275-50d2-afca-b5c3a6c0b061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[2{(3+\\frac{i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392687} {:answer/id #uuid "fa88e529-6995-5c09-a922-43fc40d4dc40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[2{(3+\\frac{3i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee49c490-8275-50d2-afca-b5c3a6c0b061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[2{(3+\\frac{i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392687} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b1fe0b7-7215-597c-b33f-addcf1c6ac8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9b0d7120-9669-5715-9447-51eb9dde3961" :question/math-academy-id "q-49179" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{3}^{4}2{x}^{2}\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{4}2{x}^{2}\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)=2{x}^{2},$ the lower bound is $a=3,$ and the upper bound is $b=4.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-3}{n}=\\frac{1}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}2{x}^{2}\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(3+i\\cdot \\frac{1}{n})\\,\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[f(3+\\frac{i}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}[2{(3+\\frac{i}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cdc82e49-5df6-5096-a8fd-e00017fb1e3a" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Definite Integral as the Limit of a Left Riemann Sum"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90ef638b-83d5-5224-a338-0b9f8dabf3c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[{(2+\\frac{l}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392690} {:answer/id #uuid "caa4420a-0661-55bb-afdb-e0dbf6ba4d43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{l}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392691} {:answer/id #uuid "3e8c75be-1194-556f-9e84-e70e9c10d0bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{2l}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392692} {:answer/id #uuid "0be90ad5-7e03-50b9-a97a-3037376e3da0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[-{(2+\\frac{l}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392693} {:answer/id #uuid "7c1f7ffb-3a77-5b4f-9e74-656e7ff5708e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{2l}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392694}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caa4420a-0661-55bb-afdb-e0dbf6ba4d43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{l}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392691} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d567818-eae9-575d-b213-daa0733bf836" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70db0eed-102a-5697-8d3f-891b9c2d06b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-49189" :question/problem "What is ${\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x$ expressed as the limit of a left Riemann sum?" :question/worked-solution "The definite integral can be defined in terms of the limit of a left Riemann sum as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\text{d}x={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{l})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhere $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ and ${x}_{l}=a+lΔx.$\n\nIn the definite integral\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nthe function is $f(x)={x}^{2},$ the lower bound is $a=1,$ and the upper bound is $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-1}{n}=\\frac{1}{n},\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{l})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[f(1+l\\cdot \\frac{1}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[f(1+\\frac{l}{n})\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}] \\\\  & ={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{\\sum }_{l=0}^{n-1}[{(1+\\frac{l}{n})}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{n}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94ad8efa-33ee-5451-b6b9-c99cb81a9ba2" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Definite Integrals of Algebraic Functions Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4025429-6e17-5c14-a483-024d71ec6616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392697} {:answer/id #uuid "906bbb28-e4b5-5434-be5a-c275368e56e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392698} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb1e0bc-fcd0-5a9a-a1c2-f002323abc31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392699} {:answer/id #uuid "1b5df1c7-ea7d-5d47-a8d0-092ad3a409bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392700} {:answer/id #uuid "d0d7aa84-cc44-5f47-a62a-eef3f56d5530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392701}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b5df1c7-ea7d-5d47-a8d0-092ad3a409bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392700} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a3d3edd-4727-5c6c-b8de-2aa598d8b805" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392696}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1acd046b-858c-598a-a588-48bb2b8b4ced" :question/math-academy-id "q-49532" :question/problem "Given that $u=3-2{x}^{2}$, which integral is equivalent to ${\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{3-2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u=3-2{x}^{2}$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4x\\,⟹\\,-\\frac{\\text{d}u}{4}=x\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe also note that ${x}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}(3-u).$ \n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $1$ | $3$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{3}\\sqrt{3-2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\sqrt{3-2{x}^{2}}\\cdot x\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{2}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\text{d}u}{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{8}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(3-u)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2a41ede-381e-55f6-99e5-1baf1ea348a1" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Integral of a Trigonometric Expression Using Integration by Parts Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7c7c20d-accc-5eb4-b6a3-26340cccb5ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392703} {:answer/id #uuid "c3276c38-5029-5b87-95b1-8d3ff7480e62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392704} {:answer/id #uuid "480dbe0b-2a18-5a64-b727-eb87c66b398a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392705} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f5ea9a-9bd8-57df-8e18-cd426e2756d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392706} {:answer/id #uuid "06683fb1-99e0-5343-bb53-9df88afcdcfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1f5ea9a-9bd8-57df-8e18-cd426e2756d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392706} :answer-field/id #uuid "1441513b-5340-5a67-a076-58e34736665d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7db8d1cc-8a1b-5f0d-8178-c39bb5e755e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-49931" :question/problem "$\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53fca396-4ade-5180-9c9b-a73f24f5b5b8" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Vector-Valued Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b57c80e-0581-56ac-b708-9d57640b62b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392710} {:answer/id #uuid "845c34dc-7482-5f11-87ee-30901151f31a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392711} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3ea727-3517-5f04-8d7e-464c04d8e2d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,-\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392712} {:answer/id #uuid "dffcd8da-e6c6-5ed5-9fd1-ef8f09f0306d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392713} {:answer/id #uuid "6ad47653-1321-5c97-9829-ac76a6e58608" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "845c34dc-7482-5f11-87ee-30901151f31a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392711} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c12cc4e-2a47-547f-be95-4a730c2736b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a4e000d9-7155-5530-bc95-f9ed61c5c6a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-50078" :question/problem "$\\int ⟨{e}^{-t},\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t=$" :question/worked-solution "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{-t},\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{-t},\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "192bb38b-b609-56ff-b560-becfc38ea070" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution of a Second Order Differential Equation by Integrating Twice"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89aee0c2-41c4-50d9-95e7-d07999f8e43b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = 5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095731} {:answer/id #uuid "a8264bab-88eb-5c1b-8cf6-4b5658e50c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y = Cx^{2} + 10x + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095732} {:answer/id #uuid "c8066636-9a63-5ade-85aa-07f7e0be5cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2} + Cx + D" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095733} {:answer/id #uuid "0a099fae-b25d-5abb-a50a-c5dc1eda7e34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y =-5x^{2}